{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "Lens flare fixture (spec 11.21). One small bright emissive quad up and to",
    "the LEFT on a near-black backdrop, which is the only configuration a ghost",
    "chain is measurable in: ghosts are the source mirrored through frame",
    "centre, so they owe the lower-right, and a scene with large bright areas",
    "would put a source in every pixel and read as a wash instead.",
    "",
    "No lights. The emitter is the whole scene, so the frame is exactly the",
    "bloom pyramid's content and nothing else can move the measurement.",
    "",
    "Bloom stays ON because the flare reads its pyramid -- there is no other",
    "thresholded image in the chain. Exposure is pinned so two runs compare."
  ],
  "models": [ { "path": "flare_fixture.gltf" } ],
  "environment": { "mode": "hdr", "intensity": 0.0 },
  "camera": { "eye": [0.0, 0.0, 5.0], "target": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "fov": 50 },
  "post": {
    "tonemap": "neutral",
    "exposure": 1.0,
    "auto_exposure": false,
    "bloom": { "enabled": true }
  }
}
